The file is the standard's own flat JSON export, included verbatim and
unmodified. CC BY-SA 4.0 permits commercial use and redistribution and requires
attribution and a licence notice in return; ShareAlike applies to adapted
material — a work built upon or modified from the standard.

What that means for this repository, concretely:

  * The requirement text is quoted, never edited. Ids, levels and wording are
    reproduced exactly as the release publishes them, so a citation resolves.
  * Any output of this product that quotes requirement text carries the
    attribution line with it (AsvsRelease.Attribution).
  * The lens table (Resources/asvs-lens.tsv) that says which entries apply
    where holds requirement IDS and our own classifications only. A table of
    ids is a collection referring to the standard; a table reproducing its text
    would be adapted material, and ShareAlike would then reach the product.
